#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168092 :tutorial/content "The derivatives of the inverse reciprocal hyperbolic functions are shown below:\n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x) & =-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}, &  & x\\in (0,1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (1,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the derivative of the base inverse reciprocal hyperbolic functions, we can differentiate combinations of these functions, by using the properties of differentiation.\n\nFor example, let's find the derivative of\n\n$$\ny = \\arsech{(-x^2)}\n$$\n\nUsing the formulas above together with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(-{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{1-{(-{x}^{2})}^{2}}}\\cdot {(-{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}\\cdot (-2x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "dc2da505-a8d0-5680-b8a0-ddeb66c32295" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5210 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
